            <ArticleTitle>[A woman with skin rash and dyspnoea].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>D1908</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present a 36-year-old woman who was born and raised in Hongkong but currently lived in the Netherlands. She was admitted with a varicella-zoster virus (VZV) primo-infection complicated by pneumonia and hepatitis. The patient was successfully treated with aciclovir. Adult VZV primo-infections are uncommon in Dutch natives but occur more often in immigrants from countries with a temperate climate where less people are infected during childhood.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
